-- title:
--   Covariance of Vélu's full-kernel quotient under coordinate changes
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $F$, $C$ a change of Weierstrass coordinates over $F$ (so $C$ has data $u \in F^{\times}$, $r, s, t \in F$), $Q$ a point of the affine curve $W$, and $N$ a natural number with $\mathrm{addOrderOf}\,Q = N$. For a Weierstrass curve $V$ over $F$, a point $P$ of $V$ and a natural number $M$, the curve `fullKernelQuotient` is Vélu's model $V.\mathrm{veluQuotientOfSums}(T, U)$, namely the curve with the same $a_1, a_2, a_3$ as $V$, with $a_4$ replaced by $a_4 - 5T$ and $a_6$ by $a_6 - b_2 T - 7U$, where $T = \sum g_x(x,y)$ and $U = \sum \bigl(x\,g_x(x,y) - y\,g_y(x,y)\bigr)$, the sums being over the finite set of coordinate pairs $(k \bullet P).\mathrm{coordsOrZero}$ for $k \in [1, M-1]$, and $g_x = 3x^2 + 2a_2x + a_4 - a_1y$, $g_y = -(2y + a_1x + a_3)$. The transported point $\mathrm{vcInvFun}\,C\,W\,Q$ on $C \bullet W$ is $0$ if $Q = 0$ and otherwise has coordinates $\bigl(u^{-2}(x-r),\, u^{-3}(y - t - s(x-r))\bigr)$. The assertion is the equality of Weierstrass curves $(C \bullet W).\mathrm{fullKernelQuotient}(\mathrm{vcInvFun}\,C\,W\,Q)\,N = C \bullet \bigl(W.\mathrm{fullKernelQuotient}\,Q\,N\bigr)$, i.e. equality of all five coefficients.
--
--   This is the covariance of Vélu's explicit quotient construction under isomorphisms of Weierstrass models: forming the quotient by the cyclic subgroup generated by a point commutes with a change of Weierstrass coordinates. It is used in the modular-curve part of the development, for instance in the comparison of moduli points attached to `fullKernelQuotient` under Atkin–Lehner involutions and in the construction of equivariant torsion reductions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_fullKernelQuotient_variableChange_vcInvFun.lean

